# {{ project_slug }}

dbt project running bronze → silver → gold transformations over the Databricks TPCH sample dataset, orchestrated by a Databricks Job (`dbt_task`) and deployed as a Databricks Asset Bundle.

## Prerequisites

- [Databricks CLI](https://docs.databricks.com/dev-tools/cli/install.html) v0.230+, authenticated (`databricks auth login`)
- A Unity Catalog-enabled workspace with access to `samples.tpch`
- Permission to create catalogs in the metastore — the bundle creates catalogs `{{ cfg.bronze_catalog }}`, `{{ cfg.silver_catalog }}`, `{{ cfg.gold_catalog }}` (or your overrides) on deploy

## What's here

```
models/
├── sources.yml         # TPCH source declarations
├── bronze/             # One view per TPCH source table
├── silver/
│   └── orders_enriched.sql   # Orders + customer/nation/region attributes resolved
└── gold/                # Star schema: dim_customer, dim_part, dim_supplier, fact_order
resources/jobs/dbt_job.yml    # Job running `dbt build` via a serverless dbt_task
dbt_project.yml               # Per-layer materialization + catalog mapping
```

## Deploy

```bash
databricks bundle validate --target dev
databricks bundle deploy --target dev
databricks bundle run {{ project_slug | replace("-", "_") }}_job --target dev
```

## Local dbt development

`profiles.yml` is provided for running dbt from your laptop against the same warehouse:

```bash
export DATABRICKS_HOST=...
export DATABRICKS_HTTP_PATH=...
export DATABRICKS_TOKEN=...
dbt build
```

## Variables

| Variable | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `bronze_catalog` | `{{ cfg.bronze_catalog }}` | Catalog for raw source views |
| `silver_catalog` | `{{ cfg.silver_catalog }}` | Catalog for cleansed/enriched tables |
| `gold_catalog` | `{{ cfg.gold_catalog }}` | Catalog for the dimensional model |

## Troubleshooting

- **"Metastore storage root URL does not exist"** — your metastore doesn't have default storage configured, so the bundle can't create the target catalogs automatically. Either enable default storage for the metastore (account console → Unity Catalog), or create one catalog manually via the UI first to provision the storage root, then redeploy.
- **`dbt build` fails locally** — check that `DATABRICKS_HOST`/`DATABRICKS_HTTP_PATH`/`DATABRICKS_TOKEN` are exported and point at a running SQL warehouse.
